<h4 local-id=3D"47ef1c5ed2e2" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-B.TechnicalImplementation:HAPIFHIRTerminologyService">=
<strong>B. Technical Implementation: HAPI FHIR Terminology Service</strong>=
</h4>
<p local-id=3D"ef3e7a8fd541">We leverage the <strong>HAPI FHIR Terminology =
Service</strong> architecture for high-performance, versioned mapping. The =
implementation uses specialized handlers inspired by standard FHIR loaders =
to process NVV-specific CSV/JSON masters.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2a673f4710b6">
<li local-id=3D"dc52305530e7">
<p local-id=3D"30e0619446e8"><strong>Dynamic ConceptMap Loading</strong>: L=
ocal masters from <code>Navavej-Data-Sharing-Package-Master.csv</code> are =
converted into FHIR <code>ConceptMap</code> resources.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"db6e007343e3">
<p local-id=3D"959132587f25"><strong>Handler Logic</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"5f3a4bfea7d9">
<li local-id=3D"de76cf2e039d">
<p local-id=3D"8630aa4dd60a"><strong>SNOMED CT Handler</strong>: Implements=
 relationship logic (ISA) and concept status tracking (Active/Inactive) as =
seen in <code>SctHandlerConcept.java</code>.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"81427051bb70">
<p local-id=3D"6234323d8964"><strong>LOINC Handler</strong>: Processes comp=
lex lab properties (CodingProperties) and linguistic variants to ensure Tha=
i common names are mapped correctly to LOINC parts.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"0b91837fd84b">
<p local-id=3D"9d07ad2c2be0"><strong>ICD-10 Loader</strong>: Utilizes <code=
>ClaML</code> (Classification Markup Language) or CSV equivalents to build =
hierarchical diagnosis trees in the Silver layer.</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h4 local-id=3D"890b5b025c2a" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-C.StandardDataProfiling(Synthea-Standardized)"><strong=
>C. Standard Data Profiling (Synthea-Standardized)</strong></h4>
<p local-id=3D"48fda25dd8b6">To validate mapping accuracy, the pipeline ben=
chmarks against standardized FHIR datasets (e.g., Synthea).</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7e60aaa63810">
<li local-id=3D"c811dab64d15">
<p local-id=3D"821a773742ca"><strong>Observation Profiling</strong>: Mappin=
g <code>pH of Urine</code> to LOINC <code>5803-2</code> and <code>BMI</code=
> to LOINC <code>59576-4</code>.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4189cb2f7945">
<p local-id=3D"b11055c0c0a0"><strong>Condition Profiling</strong>: Standard=
izing "Sepsis" to SNOMED CT <code>91302008</code>.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"4707e7a23dbc">
<p local-id=3D"c68eef11a361"><strong>Encounter Profiling</strong>: Mapping =
"Urgent care clinic" to SNOMED CT <code>185347001</code>.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"97280ed7b903">This mapping ensures that even as HIS codes ev=
olve, the AI layer interacts with an immutable, standardized Gold Layer.</p=
>
<h3 local-id=3D"31462da3d3e1" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-4.4.2Invalid&amp;MissingDataHandling(HISIntegration)">=
4.4.2 Invalid &amp; Missing Data Handling (HIS Integration)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5960bc5abf06">To maintain high data quality and system relia=
bility, the pipeline implements automated handling for common data issues f=
ound in the Navavej HIS:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1096" data-layout=3D"center" data-local-id=3D"16=
d4ae6f69fd" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 157.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 230.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 708.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"65ee032b6cc6">
<th data-local-id=3D"e7889320591d" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"d4cbc80f8f12">Data Issue</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"2f62663a4242" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"26de5a47c9de">Handling Strategy</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"9b07e5a74873" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"574cafb93949">Technical Implementation</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"54832004fbb7">
<td data-local-id=3D"bfa8207d9cda" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"13e2ed980d1c"><strong>Missing </strong><code>activeto</code>=
</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"225393f9d04d" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"058918f9b715"><strong>Persistent Defaulting</strong></p></td=
>
<td data-local-id=3D"a176c1a54925" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c874e9329096">If <code>activeto</code> is NULL (e.g., <code>=
NVV-PK-0006</code>), the pipeline defaults to <code>9999-12-31</code> to re=
present an indefinitely active package.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"0122f1d7a105">
<td data-local-id=3D"5401efca7026" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a200a2fc96fb"><strong>Thai Characters in Codes/Names</strong=
></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"86e07b0834b4" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c4cab5e4f396"><strong>UTF-8 Normalization</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"bab199b3fc7c" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"fc3cdd4bbc2e">Names like <code>TLI_=E0=B9=82=E0=B8=9B=E0=B8=
=A3=E0=B9=81=E0=B8=81=E0=B8=A3=E0=B8=A1=E0=B8=95=E0=B8=A3=E0=B8=A7=E0=B8=88=
=E0=B8=AA=E0=B8=B8=E0=B8=82=E0=B8=A0=E0=B8=B2=E0=B8=9E</code> are stored in=
 <code>Observation.code.text</code> or <code>Patient.name</code> using UTF-=
8. The <code>code</code> remains the alphanumeric NVV ID.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"5bdd3e363262">
<td data-local-id=3D"ca5ff1a4da57" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"86c79b8372b5"><strong>Invalid Date Formats</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"cc5ff3dd77ed" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"95fc2dc1e8d6"><strong>ISO 8601 Casting</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"76f7367a9169" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"cd3f3c447cd8">HIS timestamps (e.g.,<code>2026-03-16 10:50:15=
.000 +0700</code>) are cast into standard FHIR UTC format for the Silver la=
yer.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"f12b0ac01a05">
<td data-local-id=3D"b578ab14c38f" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"96e55ef8f123"><strong>Missing PII (Thai National ID)</strong=
></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"47f7b7fe34ea" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"2908592195f7"><strong>Fallback Identifier</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"75c4b121025f" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b362a044468a">If Thai National ID is missing, the system use=
s the Hospital&nbsp;<strong>Medical Record Number (MRN)</strong> as the pri=
mary FHIR identifier.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"3c074f512efc">
<td data-local-id=3D"9b3293cf40de" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"bbefa16e7e5a"><strong>Duplicate Records</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c88125caab0b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6bdfb8b606c9"><strong>Idempotent UPSERT</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"45a0ba24740c" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1bff81fed0fb">Log-based CDC ensures exactly-once processing.=
 Incoming records with existing <code>id</code> or <code>code</code> perfor=
m a versioned update (FHIR History).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"569303ad70a0">
<td data-local-id=3D"ffb0d4b783d8" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"73e6374e6bc9"><strong>Out-of-Order Events</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"d5f2261cf893" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1f3792e9bb93"><strong>Temporal Sequencing</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"35e6c63a7815" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"22c5ab8d6cc5">Using <code>effectiveTime</code> from CDC logs=
 to ensure clinical records are processed in the correct chronological orde=
r regardless of arrival time.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"700baf037b36" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-4.4.3HealthTrendPre-Computing(Velocity,Gaps,eGFRslope)=
">4.4.3 Health Trend Pre-Computing (Velocity, Gaps, eGFR slope)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a549a403d015">To optimize AI performance and ensure reliable=
 medical accuracy, raw standardized data from the Masked Silver layer under=
goes heavy transformation in the Processing engine before landing in the Go=
ld Layer. This includes basic Data Aggregation, Health Trend Calculation (e=
.g., BMI velocity, eGFR slope), and Clinical Health Gaps Analysis. Rather t=
han relying on the AI to deduce complex math on the fly, these generated fe=
atures are stored as ready-to-query assets.</p>
<h4 local-id=3D"a3d830b76f02" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-A.DataAggregation(Metrics&amp;Summaries)"><strong>A. D=
ata Aggregation (Metrics &amp; Summaries)</strong></h4>
<p local-id=3D"b224d987fc8e">Basic patient metrics and summaries are aggreg=
ated to present holistic health snapshots.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"a1387113cb24">
<li local-id=3D"916dca8a162b">
<p local-id=3D"9bde0db14be7"><strong>Implementation</strong>: Rolls up long=
itudinal lab results, vital averages over time, and active condition lists.=
 These aggregate views form the foundation of the <code>Aggregated FHIR Dat=
a</code> Gold store, directly powering BI dashboards and immediate patient =
history retrieval for the MCP server.</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 local-id=3D"e258f83e9efb" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-B.HealthTrendCalculation(Velocity&amp;Slopes)"><strong=
>B. Health Trend Calculation (Velocity &amp; Slopes)</strong></h4>
<p local-id=3D"2d5d9e655e30"><strong>eGFR Slope (Renal Function Trend):</st=
rong><br>
The eGFR slope quantifies the annual change in kidney function, serving as =
a critical surrogate endpoint for chronic kidney disease (CKD) progression.=
</p>
<ul local-id=3D"3a6b2a61b049">
<li local-id=3D"70b5cdccc027">
<p local-id=3D"d421f37a091c"><strong>Calculation Methodology</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"d2e27412b043">
<li local-id=3D"7a57b1b30248">
<p local-id=3D"081ca985b472"><strong>Algorithm</strong>: e.g. based on long=
itudinal <code>Observation</code> resources (LOINC <code>33914-3</code>, <c=
ode>98979-8</code>).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b2a7a0832466">
<p local-id=3D"e85da6354862"><strong>Minimum Data</strong>: Requires at lea=
st 2 measurements over a minimum 90-day period to establish a baseline and =
trend.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"6dc392d38aaf">
<p local-id=3D"b4e7a49cb88d"><strong>Clinical Significance</strong>: e.g. A=
 slope decline &gt; X mL/min/1.73m=C2=B2/year indicates rapid progression, =
triggering an automated clinical alert.</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"078f7f9e552d"><strong>C. BMI Velocity (Growth &amp; Metaboli=
c Trend):</strong><br>
BMI velocity tracks the rate of change in Body Mass Index, essential for id=
entifying early metabolic risks or pediatric growth anomalies.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"7fa6f12a8171">
<li local-id=3D"563601b6a448">
<p local-id=3D"9e40e1ba74a9"><strong>Calculation Methodology</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"13387e5522f4">
<li local-id=3D"eca340837246">
<p local-id=3D"99c6d756b0ef"><strong>Data Source</strong>: Calculated from =
height (LOINC <code>8302-2</code>) and weight (LOINC <code>29463-7</code>) =
observations.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"5ba18a95b276">
<p local-id=3D"28b488a49eec"><strong>Algorithm</strong>: Rolling 12-month w=
indow average.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b293a2d2f42b">
<p local-id=3D"8da74088f52b"><strong>Normalization</strong>: Adjusted for a=
ge and sex using WHO/CDC growth charts for pediatric patients.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"91f4a6c82304">
<p local-id=3D"3a1cc8d94b73"><strong>Clinical Significance</strong>: Sudden=
 spikes in BMI velocity are flagged as early indicators for metabolic syndr=
ome or obesity-related risks.</p></li>
</ul>
<h4 local-id=3D"7b2cd355b0ce" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-D.ClinicalHealthGapsAnalysis"><strong>D. Clinical Heal=
th Gaps Analysis</strong></h4>
<p local-id=3D"9c80ec9586f5">Health gaps identify discrepancies between a p=
atient's current health status and established clinical guidelines.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"bcbbdf1df494">
<li local-id=3D"66b6fd53c629">
<p local-id=3D"8ef3d51941ca"><strong>Calculation Methodology</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"97ef07f63215">
<li local-id=3D"36bd07060cd2">
<p local-id=3D"1f54cbcd45d5"><strong>Algorithm</strong>: Boolean logic matc=
hing <code>Condition</code> and <code>Procedure</code> history against <cod=
e>CarePlan</code> protocols.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"d797f1c4bd2c">
<p local-id=3D"a16c1ba890ff"><strong>FHIR Implementation</strong>: Leveragi=
ng the <code>$care-gaps</code> operation (HAPI FHIR / Clinical Reasoning mo=
dule) to detect open gaps (e.g., missing HbA1c screening for diabetic patie=
nts).</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa0c2aa8bc74">
<p local-id=3D"a3b97e85c132"><strong>Gap Types</strong>:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"6e78e528988a">
<li local-id=3D"550ca94cf31b">
<p local-id=3D"572d08116ccc"><strong>Screening Gaps</strong>: Missing age-a=
ppropriate screenings (e.g., Colonoscopy, Mammography).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"aa647fb2ce9a">
<p local-id=3D"616f571597bf"><strong>Medication Gaps</strong>: Non-adherenc=
e to chronic disease medication (e.g., Statins for CVD).</p></li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h4 local-id=3D"d3664b6fc077" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-E.TechnicalImplementation"><strong>E. Technical Implem=
entation</strong></h4>
<p local-id=3D"fb029195ccc3">We construct an automated ETL/ELT pipeline lev=
eraging <strong>Apache Spark</strong> and <strong>dbt</strong> (using <code=
>fhir-dbt-analytics</code> macros).</p>
<ul local-id=3D"2efb65bf3bb7">
<li local-id=3D"5852bc9a2f6e">
<p local-id=3D"1bdd27a07cae"><strong>Event-Driven</strong>: Micro-batch rec=
alculations of aggregations and trends are initiated by updates in the Mask=
ed Silver layer.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"e67635286099">
<p local-id=3D"9729d3f28b49"><strong>Persistence</strong>: Results from Tre=
nds and Gaps analysis are structured as engineered features and stored in t=
he <strong>Trending &amp; ML Features Gold layer</strong>, optimized for mi=
llisecond-latency retrieval by the Smart Health AI Recommendation Engine.</=
p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"44d4a99355ae" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-4.5Dual-StorageStrategy">4.5 Dual-Storage Strategy</h2=
>
<h3 local-id=3D"1b831b461f3e" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-4.5.1CoreFHIRDatabase(ImmutableClinicalRecords)">4.5.1=
 Core FHIR Database (Immutable Clinical Records)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"b0b662d40950">The Core FHIR Databases represent our <strong>=
Silver Layer</strong>, split into two distinct physical stores to ensure ab=
solute privacy:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"9e196809ab52">
<li local-id=3D"1d785ed6cd6e">
<p local-id=3D"375529fd7284"><strong>Un-Masked FHIR Store:</strong> Tempora=
rily holds standardized FHIR R4 resources containing PII in a highly restri=
cted secure enclave. Access is strictly limited to the Masking Engine and a=
uthorized break-glass services.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"08c7d7979de5">
<p local-id=3D"d5f126321c8f"><strong>Masked FHIR Store (System of Record):<=
/strong> The primary system of record for the platform. All Personally Iden=
tifiable Information (PII) is removed or tokenized via format-preserving en=
cryption prior to insertion here.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"752ccd754342">
<p local-id=3D"e7fcfa33a55c"><strong>Design Pattern:</strong> Data in both =
stores is strictly modeled as HL7 FHIR R4 JSON resources. The Masked store =
is treated as an append-only, immutable ledger ensuring exact historical cl=
inical states, full auditability, and uncompromising adherence to PDPA regu=
lations.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"25a398150f04" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-4.5.2Pre-AggregatedLakehouse(Trending&amp;MLFeatures)"=
>4.5.2 Pre-Aggregated Lakehouse (Trending &amp; ML Features)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"775704b77c20">The Lakehouse represents our <strong>Gold Laye=
r</strong>, optimized exclusively for high-speed analytical reads, complex =
longitudinal queries, and AI feature serving.</p>
<ul local-id=3D"76ca8c822644">
<li local-id=3D"78c3b64b8ece">
<p local-id=3D"18a07dea9953"><strong>Design Pattern:</strong> Optimized for=
 heavy read-access, time-series querying, and columnar analytics rather tha=
n transactional clinical updates.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"08814a9542ec">
<p local-id=3D"14da74674b2b"><strong>Purpose:</strong> It holds the pre-agg=
regated metrics, statistical gaps, and engineered features (like health vel=
ocity and moving averages). This allows the application layer, BI Dashboard=
s, and AI models to retrieve rich patient context with millisecond latency =
without querying the Core FHIR Database.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"5f4c87b1d724" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-5.DataPlatformTechStack">5. Data Platform Tech Stack</=
h2>
<p local-id=3D"878903b804e0">Our solution is flexible and can be deployed u=
tilizing either AWS Managed Services or an Open-Source Hybrid approach:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"760" data-layout=3D"default" data-local-id=3D"d5=
288f00aa0a" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"a17716c014a7">
<th data-local-id=3D"01d0c37ace59" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"0f764d824a44">Component Category</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"3400b24e7194" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"05f83638f66e">AWS Cloud Strategy</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"a11bd9b82c2c" class=3D"confluenceTh">
<p local-id=3D"87f2714d80c4">Open Source / Hybrid Strategy</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"9bc56f95fe6c">
<td data-local-id=3D"fcda27da66bd" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"c28f011dec26"><strong>Ingestion &amp; CDC</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c068f8a75630" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0ff91493dace">AWS DMS (Database Migration Service) or Manage=
d Kafka (MSK).</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"733d1f86ce5e" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"65f863457849">Debezium and Apache Kafka.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"67e5e1ad4d9a">
<td data-local-id=3D"e02ae4a068df" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"4752c0bd5297"><strong>Data Storage (Bronze/Silver/Gold)</str=
ong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"4181e89db84b" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"dcfb62418f03">Amazon S3 (Bronze), AWS HealthLake (Native FHI=
R Silver Layer - separated into isolated Un-Masked and Masked instances), a=
nd Amazon Redshift / Athena (Gold/Trending Store).</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"84a658ccf679" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0b100cc02a63">MinIO (S3-compatible Bronze), HAPI FHIR backed=
 by PostgreSQL (Silver Layer - with logically separated Un-Masked and Maske=
d schemas), and ClickHouse (High-performance Gold/Trending Store).</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ca4604b6da83">
<td data-local-id=3D"18083ce67ab1" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"3bb81d78d388"><strong>Processing, Orchestration &amp; PII Ma=
sking</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"56cd77141052" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"557063283f8e">AWS Lambda / AWS Macie for dynamic masking and=
 PII tokenization, AWS Glue / EMR (Apache Spark) for ETL and trend pre-comp=
utation.</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"e77f73b8ef55" class=3D"confluenceTd">
<p local-id=3D"edcfa3889690">Apache Airflow / Temporal for orchestration, A=
pache Flink / Baffle for real-time masking, and dbt for metric aggregations=
.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"736d4b919b77">
<td data-local-id=3D"75d24f15d646" class=3D"confluenceTd">
