<h1 local-id=3D"27beadbdc3d3" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.Security,Privacy&amp;DataGovernance"><strong>6. Secu=
rity, Privacy &amp; Data Governance</strong></h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"c51cad517df2" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.1SMARTonFHIRAuthorization(AccessControlGatekeeper)">=
6.1 SMART on FHIR Authorization (Access Control Gatekeeper)</h2>
<p local-id=3D"3a61e608580c">To guarantee absolute compliance with PDPA and=
 healthcare privacy standards, the system implements the <strong>SMART on F=
HIR</strong> framework as the definitive security gatekeeper for all clinic=
al data. This ensures that no system component=E2=80=94whether it is a doct=
or=E2=80=99s dashboard or the AI Model Context Protocol (MCP) server=E2=80=
=94can access the FHIR Database without explicitly granted, resource-level =
permissions.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"8ff61dd1b46a" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.1.1High-LevelArchitecture&amp;IdentityIntegration">6=
.1.1 High-Level Architecture &amp; Identity Integration</h3><span class=3D"=
confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embedded-m=
anual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=3D"nv=
v-smart-auth.jpeg" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"8f46eb7513ab6ddd87=
6ee2889860ca7931a14bd0ffbc5b3ab397a2b3f7f02e3e" data-image-src=3D"https://v=
ns-site.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/237994005/nvv-smart-auth.jp=
eg?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1774280972738&amp;cacheVersion=3D1&am=
p;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"1536" data-width=3D"2816" data-unresolved-commen=
t-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"240451586" data-linked-resource-ve=
rsion=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" data-linked-resource-d=
efault-alias=3D"nvv-smart-auth.jpeg" data-base-url=3D"https://vns-site.atla=
ssian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=3D"image/jpeg" data-linke=
d-resource-container-id=3D"237994005" data-linked-resource-container-versio=
n=3D"65" data-media-id=3D"a4f9c04a-581c-47ba-a7c7-03fb9862357a" data-media-=
type=3D"file" height=3D"255"></span>
<ul local-id=3D"e3063d3d-3fa8-434f-87eb-369798230ed1">
<li local-id=3D"7f8df385-ea87-419f-a414-516593986d33">
<p local-id=3D"53b535673051"><strong>OAuth 2.0 &amp; Identity Provider (IdP=
) Integration:</strong> The Authorization Server integrates seamlessly with=
 Navavej Hospital's existing Identity Provider (e.g., Active Directory, Key=
cloak, or Okta) using standard OAuth 2.0 and OpenID Connect (OIDC). For thi=
s platform to operate effectively, the hospital's chosen IdP must satisfy t=
wo strict SMART-compliance constraints:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"635b57ed-40a4-43a9-880f-e3d350a702d0">
<li local-id=3D"bb1f9271-5336-4c4c-9d49-50961d495557">
<p local-id=3D"25e559651957"><strong>Define Custom Scopes:</strong> The IdP=
 must natively support scopes containing special characters required by FHI=
R routing logic (e.g., <code>patient/*.read</code> or <code>launch/patient<=
/code>).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"2242d3bc-2cc4-4c1a-9c3a-422751d96536">
<p local-id=3D"8a14ef2bbe05"><strong>Inject Custom Claims:</strong> The IdP=
 must allow the dynamic injection of custom data claims (such as passing a =
specific patient ID or the <code>fhirUser</code> URL) directly into the JWT=
 Access Token before it reaches the FHIR server.</p></li>
</ol></li>
<li local-id=3D"77e01e1f-8031-4a9d-bb97-4bcefea530a9">
<p local-id=3D"e3974a114cf2"><strong>Secure Token Relay (On-Behalf-Of Flow)=
:</strong> The architecture utilizes a highly secure, consistent token rela=
y to guarantee that AI inferences always respect human access rights across=
 all microservices:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"764e59f3-44d0-4491-b917-b1f5e702430b">
<li local-id=3D"2085c5ef-44bc-4312-8d4a-21705771e328">
<p local-id=3D"bd4a77870a79"><strong>Authentication:</strong> A doctor acce=
sses the Web Dashboard and authenticates with the IdP, obtaining an active =
user session containing a scoped SMART on FHIR access token.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9a6e19a2-bbd0-4605-af8b-cd14cfbfcccc">
<p local-id=3D"df8f04b8c21f"><strong>Recommendation Request:</strong> The d=
ashboard passes the request <em>along with the doctor's specific session to=
ken</em> to the central backend <strong>Hybrid Recommendation Engine</stron=
g>.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"3577d685-a5b4-4d2e-a777-96cee9a6c39b">
<p local-id=3D"a7373dfa0aa7"><strong>Context Fetching:</strong> The Hybrid =
Engine delegates the data-gathering workload to the <strong>MCP Server</str=
ong>, passing the user token forward.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6437de44-bcc9-44d5-865b-8d947280dee7">
<p local-id=3D"bb59a7f843e9"><strong>SMART Authorization Gate:</strong> Rat=
her than using an over-privileged generic system password, the MCP presents=
 the doctor's exact session token to the SMART Auth Server. This conclusive=
ly proves the components are fetching data strictly <em>on behalf of</em> t=
he authorized physician.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f1491582-b5fb-48d8-b495-9e87ab17b366">
<p local-id=3D"e4258855a182"><strong>Data Delivery &amp; Masking:</strong> =
Upon validating the token's scopes and signatures, the SMART server permits=
 the MCP to safely extract the required records from the Core FHIR Database=
 (<code>clinical_fhir</code>) . The MCP then scrubs and masks the PII <em>b=
efore</em> the Hybrid Engine ever passes it to the Central AI Gateway for e=
xternal LLM inference.</p></li>
</ol></li>
</ul>
<blockquote local-id=3D"8646befe8498">
<p local-id=3D"a079a2ede3bc"><strong>Design Note =E2=80=94 Session &amp; To=
ken Lifetime:</strong> The On-Behalf-Of token relay operates exclusively in=
 a <strong>user-initiated context</strong>. AI recommendations are generate=
d only when a Healthcare Provider explicitly triggers the recommendation wo=
rkflow from the active dashboard session. There are no background, batch, o=
r scheduled AI inference jobs that operate without an active user session. =
The SMART on FHIR session timeout is configured at <strong>30 minutes</stro=
ng>, providing ample headroom above the maximum end-to-end SLA target of <s=
trong>30 seconds</strong> per inference request. Token expiry during infere=
nce is therefore not a practical risk.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 local-id=3D"420c73ead75e" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.1.2TechnicalBenefits&amp;SecurityExplanations">6.1.2=
 Technical Benefits &amp; Security Explanations</h3>
<p local-id=3D"1bb437d6817b">Adopting the SMART on FHIR standard provides s=
weeping technical advantages over traditional API security models:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"4ce938dc-dd76-4635-b5b8-b149c3b77233">
<li local-id=3D"ed98557e-a8ee-46cb-b664-6874268511d1">
<p local-id=3D"37c30e9e7a0e"><strong>Granular "Least Privilege" Scopes</str=
ong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1d09bc12b688">
<li local-id=3D"e6b97f9a2995">
<p local-id=3D"8edd1c5e7c12">Traditional systems often grant generic "API a=
ccess" to an entire database. SMART on FHIR utilizes highly granular clinic=
al scopes (e.g., <code>patient/Observation.read</code>). This means the MCP=
 Server can be authorized to read a patient's lab results (Observations) to=
 generate a recommendation, without ever having the technical permission to=
 read their psychiatric notes or billing information.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"c367b4dc-4169-4afd-baa0-7e0c5527cf83">
<p local-id=3D"c8fb3e1a9f8b"><strong>Secure Launch Context (Seamless UX)</s=
trong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"84921ac85bee">
<li local-id=3D"45a71fee19d8">
<p local-id=3D"616b20fb1cdd">The standard perfectly supports "EHR Launch" s=
equences. If a physician opens our new Recommendation Dashboard directly fr=
om inside the legacy Navavej HIS, SMART on FHIR seamlessly passes the activ=
e <code>patient_id</code> and security token to our app. The doctor does no=
t need to log in a second time or manually search for the patient again, dr=
astically improving user adoption.</p></li>
</ul></li>
<li local-id=3D"0510815a-56d1-4b2f-a018-21ecfe4bbb68">
<p local-id=3D"1ef0c914a642"><strong>Open-Source Reliability</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"da2bf7e3fa68">
<li local-id=3D"d83f1144904e">
<p local-id=3D"3e7532a7d8c9">Because SMART on FHIR is a global healthcare I=
T standard, Navavej is not locked into proprietary security logic. The engi=
neering team will leverage battle-tested open-source libraries (such as tho=
se from SMART Health IT) to handle the complex token handshakes, ensuring e=
nterprise-grade security while accelerating the development timeline.</p></=
li>
</ul></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"0c270b86605a" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.2DataMasking&amp;Pseudo-AnonymizationPipelines">6.2 =
Data Masking &amp; Pseudo-Anonymization Pipelines</h2>
<p local-id=3D"a214b6e76ce2">To meet the strict <code>&lt; 10-second</code>=
 latency SLA (per TOR =C2=A76.3), minimize cloud infrastructure costs, and =
guarantee PDPA/HIPAA compliance, the system adopts an <strong>Asynchronous =
Pre-Masking Architecture</strong> as its primary data protection strategy. =
Clinical data is scrubbed of all Personally Identifiable Information (PII) =
at ingestion time=E2=80=94well before AI inference=E2=80=94rather than rely=
ing on real-time, on-the-fly masking during the critical request path. This=
 architectural decision is driven by the computational cost of Thai-languag=
e NLP processing, the fail-safe behavior it guarantees, and the auditabilit=
y requirements of PDPA.</p>
<blockquote local-id=3D"a9db9f4f-77af-4240-a72e-1ff80e72f5f5">
<p local-id=3D"b5a6464c68ab"><strong>Clarification on MCP's Role:</strong> =
In this architecture, the MCP Server operates as a <strong>read-only data a=
ccessor</strong> that queries the pre-masked schema exclusively. It does no=
t perform real-time PII scrubbing itself. All NLP-based masking is complete=
d asynchronously by the Data Masking Pipeline before any AI inference reque=
st occurs.</p>
</blockquote>
<h3 local-id=3D"fd416aa06d78" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.2.1UnifiedCompute,PartitionedStorageArchitecture">6.=
2.1 Unified Compute, Partitioned Storage Architecture</h3>
<p local-id=3D"da4f90ccb86f">To reduce cloud infrastructure costs without s=
acrificing security, the architecture avoids deploying two separate physica=
l database servers. Instead, it utilizes a single, unified database cluster=
 (e.g., PostgreSQL) divided by strict logical schemas with independent acce=
ss controls.</p>
<p local-id=3D"34469b191405">The Data Integration Pipeline standardizes raw=
 medical data into the protected <code>clinical_fhir</code> schema. Immedia=
tely after ingestion, an asynchronous background job runs the data through =
the NLP-based Pre-Masking Pipeline, writing the scrubbed results into an is=
olated <code>masked_clinical_fhir</code> schema on the same server. When th=
e MCP tool (e.g., <code>getMaskedData?patient_id=3D123</code>) is invoked d=
uring AI inference, it fetches context exclusively from this pre-scrubbed s=
chema - never from the raw <code>clinical_fhir</code> schema.</p><span clas=
s=3D"confluence-embedded-file-wrapper image-center-wrapper confluence-embed=
ded-manual-size"><img class=3D"confluence-embedded-image image-center" alt=
=3D"nvv-masked-data-flow.jpeg" width=3D"468" loading=3D"lazy" src=3D"a7dc4e=
ce774cb2bc9408a0fedbabb7122a955fef773b8b7e6464619532cb5087" data-image-src=
=3D"https://vns-site.atlassian.net/wiki/download/attachments/237994005/nvv-=
masked-data-flow.jpeg?version=3D1&amp;modificationDate=3D1774281085815&amp;=
cacheVersion=3D1&amp;api=3Dv2" data-height=3D"1536" data-width=3D"2816" dat=
a-unresolved-comment-count=3D"0" data-linked-resource-id=3D"240418824" data=
-linked-resource-version=3D"1" data-linked-resource-type=3D"attachment" dat=
a-linked-resource-default-alias=3D"nvv-masked-data-flow.jpeg" data-base-url=
=3D"https://vns-site.atlassian.net/wiki" data-linked-resource-content-type=
=3D"image/jpeg" data-linked-resource-container-id=3D"237994005" data-linked=
-resource-container-version=3D"65" data-media-id=3D"acabfe02-78c2-4020-8850=
-b743fa31588e" data-media-type=3D"file" height=3D"255"></span>
<ul local-id=3D"f21517cea785">
<li local-id=3D"1b518819-bd91-40fd-9bc3-d4171b3bdbac">
<p local-id=3D"1db06de4db3f"><strong>Microsoft Presidio &amp; PyThaiNLP Int=
egration:</strong> Because Navavej Hospital serves Thai patients, standard =
English-focused NLP masking tools are fundamentally insufficient. This pipe=
line explicitly implements <strong>Microsoft Presidio</strong> (the enterpr=
ise-grade OSS standard for PII redaction) customized with <strong>PyThaiNLP=
</strong>. This guarantees the accurate detection, tokenization, and redact=
ion of Thai names, residential addresses, and National ID patterns hidden w=
ithin free-text medical notes.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"30ac7867e833" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.2.2Freshness-GapHandling(HybridSafetyNet)">6.2.2 Fre=
shness-Gap Handling (Hybrid Safety Net)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"e692dd8140c6">Because the Pre-Masking Pipeline operates asyn=
chronously, there is an inherent <strong>freshness gap</strong>=E2=80=94a b=
rief window (typically seconds to a few minutes) between when new raw data =
arrives via CDC sync and when its masked counterpart becomes available in t=
he <code>masked_clinical_fhir</code> schema. To handle this edge case safel=
y, the system applies a <strong>two-tier masking strategy</strong>:</p>
<div>
We don't have a way to export this macro.
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-1546305280" class=3D"expand-container">
<div id=3D"expander-control-1546305280" class=3D"expand-control">
<span class=3D"expand-control-icon"><img style=3D"vertical-align:middle;" c=
lass=3D"expand-control-image" src=3D"12d6790ad24896d77c6798d608975ef510283c=
c49b55e6f0ab90f21b044efffb" width=3D"16" height=3D"16"></span><span class=
=3D"expand-control-text">mermaid</span>
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-content-1546305280" class=3D"expand-content">
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">flowcha=
rt TD
    Request["MCP receives AI context request&lt;br&gt;for Patient X"] --&gt=
; Check{"Does masked_clinical_fhir&lt;br&gt;contain latest records&lt;br&gt=
;for Patient X?"}

    Check --&gt;|"YES (99% of requests)"| UseMasked["=E2=9C=85 Return pre-m=
asked data&lt;br&gt;Full NLP-quality masking"]
    Check --&gt;|"NO (fresh data not yet masked)"| Fallback["=E2=9A=A0=EF=
=B8=8F Apply deterministic&lt;br&gt;field-level stripping"]

    Fallback --&gt; Strip["Remove structured PII fields:&lt;br&gt;=E2=80=A2=
 patient.name =E2=86=92 [REDACTED]&lt;br&gt;=E2=80=A2 patient.birthDate =E2=
=86=92 age only&lt;br&gt;=E2=80=A2 patient.identifier =E2=86=92 removed&lt;=
br&gt;=E2=80=A2 patient.address =E2=86=92 removed&lt;br&gt;=E2=80=A2 note/t=
ext fields =E2=86=92 EXCLUDED entirely"]
    Strip --&gt; Flag["Flag response as&lt;br&gt;'partially-masked' in audi=
t log"]
    Flag --&gt; Return["Return safe payload&lt;br&gt;to Central AI Gateway"=
]
    UseMasked --&gt; Return</pre>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1049" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"7f969fa6-9bdf-4c11-a41b-bcd9288b16d4" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"01af527d-50f8-4e20-8054-a5a0aabf9286">
<th data-local-id=3D"2cb091b4-7cc9-4bd9-8095-5dcb6a157b97" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"186fc9b8d385">Tier</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"8a7cf8f8-739a-423b-881e-52a3f11abc62" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"e0f412b021b3">Trigger Condition</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"f9a68286-a8ae-4796-8bd4-0aa49fbb7493" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"928cc5194acd">Masking Method</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"e032c596-d710-4dd0-962d-23d4f40151ea" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"fc037343aa1b">Coverage</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"91c8655f-16ec-47ca-a55c-f237651330f3">
<td data-local-id=3D"b36dd6cc-2e17-4523-afef-1fec509137cc" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"12cc9218568d"><strong>Primary (Tier 1)</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"9bf4eee9-9db3-418d-9d37-621a6917e805" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8793359472f6">Masked copy exists and is up-to-date</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"98b6b2d8-fa52-4c48-b6bf-0237a77b1729" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"90268fe0d3aa">Full Presidio + PyThaiNLP NLP pipeline</p></td=
>
<td data-local-id=3D"78c2f9d5-b89b-45cb-9f13-aa473b255b4c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"d24bd1077953">Complete =E2=80=94 structured fields + free-te=
xt</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"c24392b9-9aba-420d-8719-71fc9a892fb2">
<td data-local-id=3D"45120b5d-cd72-43c8-b0bc-8616966b4f5c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7f72ca88e4bb"><strong>Fallback (Tier 2)</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"6e101627-ad32-4b5b-81f7-26e2a3fe026c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e57fc37f8944">New data arrived but masked copy not yet avail=
able</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"a7da63ba-66e3-43f0-b85a-f3ced37b6e16" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9c70fc79715e">Deterministic field-level stripping (no NLP)</=
p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"9c6f4d9b-a7a9-4ea1-a4e4-f04584780dcc" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e994a6308053">Structured fields only =E2=80=94 free-text fie=
lds are excluded entirely rather than partially masked</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<ul local-id=3D"69abfcfd-196a-489f-8b4f-847eff7c61cc">
<li local-id=3D"1e791a6b-ac76-4752-ace8-5cac15b91598">
<p local-id=3D"584505495e57"><strong>Why exclude free-text in the fallback?=
</strong> Free-text clinical notes (physician memos, nursing notes) are the=
 highest-risk PII source and require full NLP processing for safe redaction=
. Rather than attempting fast but unreliable masking under time pressure, t=
he fallback tier omits free-text entirely, accepting a minor reduction in A=
I context quality in exchange for guaranteed PII safety. The AI Gateway log=
s this as a reduced-context inference for audit transparency.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7a1e109b-bae9-43f2-80b5-77533a39d7d8">
<p local-id=3D"a0ed584e6eef"><strong>Fail-Safe Guarantee:</strong> If both =
tiers fail (e.g., database connectivity issues), the MCP returns an empty p=
ayload. The Hybrid Recommendation Engine then falls back to its determinist=
ic Safety Rules (rule-based only, no AI), ensuring the system never stalls =
and PII never leaks.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"030cc0332ca5" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.2.3TechnicalBenefits&amp;CostOptimization">6.2.3 Tec=
hnical Benefits &amp; Cost Optimization</h3>
<p local-id=3D"4b1a97f5030f">Adopting pre-masking with a deterministic fall=
back provides the following advantages over a pure real-time masking approa=
ch:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"182c4c23-9a53-4ec1-af17-d73c2712ff13">
<li local-id=3D"350fbcb2-9a00-497d-9c7b-f10e77dcdc81">
<p local-id=3D"cf1b62433ded"><strong>SLA-Safe Inference Path:</strong> Thai=
-language NLP masking (word segmentation + NER) on multi-year clinical hist=
ories is computationally expensive (estimated 1=E2=80=935 seconds per patie=
nt context). Pre-masking removes this cost entirely from the inference crit=
ical path, preserving the full <code>&lt; 10-second</code> SLA budget for a=
ctual AI reasoning.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"600487ef-1871-42fb-bb7a-5b655fb7d1e1">
<p local-id=3D"8537b538b69a"><strong>Infrastructure Cost Efficiency:</stron=
g> Schema-level separation within a single PostgreSQL instance means Navave=
j pays only for the incremental disk storage of the masked copy (~2=C3=97 c=
linical text storage), avoiding the compute cost (vCPU/RAM) of a second ded=
icated database server or a real-time NLP processing cluster.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"272c0f7d-5dcd-4b90-afb0-87af9abd0e6c">
<p local-id=3D"332ae1456386"><strong>Role-Based Access "Air Gap":</strong> =
The two schemas are separated by strict Role-Based Access Control (RBAC). T=
he MCP Server database credentials are granted <code>SELECT</code> access e=
xclusively on <code>masked_clinical_fhir</code> and explicitly <code>DENIED=
</code> on <code>clinical_fhir</code>. Even in the event of a prompt-inject=
ion attack reaching the MCP layer, the database enforces the boundary =E2=
=80=94 the MCP cannot technically query raw PII data.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"263466d4-e041-4139-8eab-92c9bc566376">
<p local-id=3D"aae86cdf052d"><strong>Deterministic &amp; Auditable Masking:=
</strong> Unlike asking an LLM to "mask the patient's name" at inference ti=
me (which is non-deterministic and prone to hallucination), the Presidio + =
PyThaiNLP pipeline is deterministic. The same input always produces the sam=
e masked output. Furthermore, the masked data is persisted in the <code>mas=
ked_clinical_fhir</code> schema, enabling auditors and DPOs to inspect exac=
tly what context the AI received for any historical inference =E2=80=94 a k=
ey PDPA compliance requirement.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"7970932e-60ea-4089-b458-e3cd27adbfd4">
<p local-id=3D"47fd55dfba76"><strong>Accurate Thai PII Detection:</strong> =
PyThaiNLP's dictionary-based and statistical word segmentation handles the =
unique challenges of Thai text (no whitespace, complex compound words) far =
more reliably than general-purpose LLM instructions. This ensures consisten=
t detection of Thai names (=E0=B8=8A=E0=B8=B7=E0=B9=88=E0=B8=AD-=E0=B8=99=
=E0=B8=B2=E0=B8=A1=E0=B8=AA=E0=B8=81=E0=B8=B8=E0=B8=A5), National ID patter=
ns (=E0=B9=80=E0=B8=A5=E0=B8=82=E0=B8=9A=E0=B8=B1=E0=B8=95=E0=B8=A3=E0=B8=
=9B=E0=B8=A3=E0=B8=B0=E0=B8=8A=E0=B8=B2=E0=B8=8A=E0=B8=99 13 =E0=B8=AB=E0=
=B8=A5=E0=B8=B1=E0=B8=81), and Thai address formats (=E0=B8=97=E0=B8=B5=E0=
=B9=88=E0=B8=AD=E0=B8=A2=E0=B8=B9=E0=B9=88) in clinical free-text.</p></li>
</ul>
<h2 local-id=3D"7091bd9b0abe" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3ComprehensiveAuditLogging">6.3 Comprehensive Audit =
Logging</h2>
<p local-id=3D"af33f71ed064">To satisfy PDPA and HIPAA requirements for a c=
linical AI system, every AI inference operation and physician decision is c=
aptured in an immutable, cryptographically protected audit log. The log is =
written <strong>synchronously before any recommendation response is deliver=
ed</strong> =E2=80=94 guaranteeing that no inference is ever unrecorded.</p=
>
<h3 local-id=3D"3987a8e977c7" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3.15-DimensionLogStructure">6.3.1 5-Dimension Log St=
ructure</h3>
<p local-id=3D"731b3da87a4b">Every audit entry is structured around five ma=
ndatory dimensions:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1011" data-layout=3D"center" data-local-id=3D"b7=
cbff0f-b40d-4592-b7cf-06ccf3003d94" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 95.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 399.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 515.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"3b4a3320-fd3c-43bc-a50b-f0728d1258b1">
<th data-local-id=3D"adcf6260-d914-4a04-b2c6-0b6c262985a0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"e5f656e0e732">Dimension</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"556aa83d-b322-43e2-a9b9-b69432219b22" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"aead963d9fd4">Fields Captured</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"cfb7beb3-c47a-40fc-994a-5732cd86334d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"a52da8ccd241">Purpose</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"e6c57961-6cd0-47c7-8e78-ca593e0ce6db">
<td data-local-id=3D"5cb9ab26-675b-425f-96f8-f8cc2e31d99d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6fb912d825de"><strong>Who</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"63d64784-55c2-4f8b-99e7-351c746f2ca9" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"887db26ff6a7"><code>user_id</code>, <code>user_role</code></=
p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"8cdf9ccf-f218-41ce-8d3a-211d654ebefa" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"52e223ec3815">Identity and role of the healthcare staff who =
triggered the inference (e.g., physician, nurse, pharmacist)</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"d7be1a23-5d07-4434-bc80-3d5fd3de5646">
<td data-local-id=3D"4c5b9678-7ae8-4eb7-a1a2-509b0234b9e3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"786d6b5273b5"><strong>When</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"00e22e66-f5e2-466f-b325-958722cce508" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"64fe7891cea5"><code>timestamp</code> (ISO 8601, UTC)</p></td=
>
<td data-local-id=3D"c7581573-3d04-4776-8882-21afd574403c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a82b5569cd12">Precise moment of the inference or clinical de=
cision event</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"02206ceb-d60a-4fef-9a0b-3ded50c961d7">
<td data-local-id=3D"d9b5cd2a-0845-4894-ae8b-7ff32a735b5a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"4538fa848975"><strong>Where</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"559df328-e26c-4144-9b7b-58a742daaf19" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b46ff0e07077"><code>service_id</code>, <code>client_ip</code=
>, <code>request_id</code></p></td>
