</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"d474dc712d24" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3.2Immutability:SHA-256HashChaining">6.3.2 Immutabil=
ity: SHA-256 Hash Chaining</h3>
<p local-id=3D"8b4afdd23889">Immutability is enforced through cryptographic=
 hash chaining. Each log entry computes:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">current=
_hash =3D SHA-256(previous_entry_hash + current_payload)</pre>
</div>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"5314be32b85d">The chain is anchored by a known genesis hash.=
 Any post-write modification =E2=80=94 including deletion, reordering, or c=
ontent edits =E2=80=94 produces a detectable hash mismatch across all subse=
quent entries. This provides tamper-evidence without requiring an external =
blockchain or notarization service.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"c72747c95311" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3.3PhysicianDecisionLogging">6.3.3 Physician Decisio=
n Logging</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5dfdf162ab7d">Approval and Rejection decisions by healthcare=
 providers are recorded as a distinct event type. Each decision entry is li=
nked to the original AI recommendation via a <code>recommendation_reference=
_hash</code>, creating a fully traceable audit trail:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">Clinica=
l Data =E2=86=92 AI Inference =E2=86=92 Human Review =E2=86=92 Final Decisi=
on</pre>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"b1bbc5962e32" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3.4PIIEnforcement">6.3.4 PII Enforcement</h3>
<p local-id=3D"e7f3a33451d6">Patient-identifiable fields are <strong>scrubb=
ed</strong> from all clinical data <strong>at ingestion time</strong> =E2=
=80=94 not at inference time =E2=80=94 by the asynchronous Pre-Masking Pipe=
line (Presidio + PyThaiNLP), which writes de-identified records into the is=
olated <code>masked_clinical_fhir</code> schema. The MCP Server reads exclu=
sively from this pre-scrubbed schema, ensuring the AI inference pipeline on=
ly ever operates on de-identified clinical signals. No PII is substituted, =
tokenised, or rehydrated within the backend at any stage of the AI workflow=
. Patient identity is resolved solely by the frontend at display time, usin=
g a secure SMART on FHIR-scoped lookup against the <code>clinical_fhir</cod=
e> schema =E2=80=94 a path that is architecturally separated from and never=
 intersects with the AI pipeline.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"c05e515baae0" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3.5Retention">6.3.5 Retention</h3>
<p local-id=3D"cb9744268b3d">All audit records must be retained for a minim=
um of <strong>3 years</strong> per PDPA Section 40. Specify storage infrast=
ructure, cold-tier archival strategy (e.g., object storage lifecycle rules =
after 6 months), and automated purge/archival mechanism at the 3-year mark.=
</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"f434e6ab02c7" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-6.3.6AccessControl">6.3.6 Access Control</h3>
<p local-id=3D"96e15830e4f2">Read access to audit logs is restricted to the=
 <strong>DPO</strong> and <strong>System Admin</strong> roles. Clinical sta=
ff (physician, nurse, pharmacist) cannot query or export audit records dire=
ctly.</p>
<p local-id=3D"d5d74688e83b">Refer to with <a href=3D"https://vns-site.atla=
ssian.net/wiki/spaces/~71202072744c7d230748d9bfcebba4c675b84a/pages/2379940=
05/Technical+Proposal+-+Smart+Health+Checkup+Recommendation+Dashboard#6.1-S=
MART-on-FHIR-Authorization-(Access-Control-Gatekeeper)" rel=3D"nofollow">=
=C2=A76.1.</a></p>
<h1 local-id=3D"cfce508fce0b" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.AI&amp;RecommendationEngineArchitecture"><strong>7. =
AI &amp; Recommendation Engine Architecture</strong></h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"0e5f9be4ee91" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.1High-LevelAIWorkflow">7.1 High-Level AI Workflow</h=
2>
<p local-id=3D"d47e6fb71b06">The AI recommendation pipeline is orchestrated=
 as a four-phase asynchronous loop. To balance inference quality against la=
tency and cost, the pipeline supports two complementary execution paths tha=
t converge on the same three-agent chain.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"6f11f7e325e6" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.1.1Two-PathDesign">7.1.1 Two-Path Design</h3>
<p local-id=3D"2612d9eaa246"><strong>Optimization Path (default)</strong> =
=E2=80=94 For cases where the standard clinical data set is sufficient, fou=
r MCP context tools are fetched in parallel upfront. If the assembled conte=
xt is deemed complete, the pipeline proceeds directly to the agent chain wi=
th no additional tool calls.</p>
<p local-id=3D"86e8b0f3991d"><strong>ReAct Path (data-gap cases)</strong> =
=E2=80=94 When the AI determines that the prefetched context is insufficien=
t for a high-quality recommendation, it issues additional targeted MCP tool=
 calls before proceeding. The number of additional calls is bounded by a co=
nfigured iteration cap to prevent unbounded latency.</p>
<p local-id=3D"dd98e13dc7e8">Both paths converge at Agent 1 and follow the =
same agent chain and post-processing steps from that point forward.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"9e32edb06a3d" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.1.2Four-PhasePipeline">7.1.2 Four-Phase Pipeline</h3=
>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1233" data-layout=3D"center" data-local-id=3D"80=
f240dd-75bb-4a3e-9d87-ce6eb497c2b7" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 236.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 618.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 377.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"869335c2-1b72-4f36-afdf-0bc6d4f34d31">
<th data-local-id=3D"2e69c87e-ea77-44ee-83c1-151036f78dcb" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"03165fe8e1e0">Phase</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"22cf5ad0-7469-4399-8e38-3d9ce4e0b374" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"548b64ed8d15">Steps</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"3ffa037d-daf1-4647-b942-a7399197b40e" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"a42a1dc0f754">Notes</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"7802668a-5466-4893-822d-6e8837c30fcd">
<td data-local-id=3D"5de49c45-e3e5-49f6-8f78-af1be43b0ce9" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7ebb40d04adf"><strong>Phase 1 =E2=80=94 Context Fetch</stron=
g></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"0b7242b9-8704-4794-9785-c792016fc55b" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ebd16e958aea">4 MCP tools called in parallel (<code>get_hard=
_constraints</code>, <code>get_clinical_signals</code>, <code>get_biomarker=
_trends</code>, <code>get_program_ruleset</code>)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"94405121-1d4f-420c-b80b-d9831fc41bf9" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a3201aab133f">No ordering dependency between tools; all resu=
lts assembled before proceeding</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"7cb3abb5-dcd0-4778-b8a1-83ad191da9e5">
<td data-local-id=3D"004edf0f-1b14-4dce-9233-63d8bb1ad257" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"5a0739953691"><strong>Phase 2 =E2=80=94 Rule Evaluation + Ag=
ent 1</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"a96eccc4-b9fc-47e9-bfa8-87e40024ae24" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"e8ccdc7a5733">Deterministic rule tier computed from active s=
ignals; Agent 1 (<code>AnalyzeClinicalRisks</code>) produces a structured c=
linical risk profile</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"292aa61c-c6ba-442a-9178-eabb001bd5a3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1b5864155fd0">Agent 1 failure triggers immediate full rule-b=
ased fallback</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"e55b5cbf-ca52-4e5e-b997-c8f2bba4c0d4">
<td data-local-id=3D"1c6a2aae-6cdf-4a7d-85a8-8e604bf9146f" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"2c5953e3fa05"><strong>Phase 3 =E2=80=94 Agent 2a + Agent 2b =
(parallel)</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"6ffbe424-e026-44fc-ad5b-43806a5752d2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"59943e8177f9">Agent 2a (<code>MatchPolicy</code>) selects pr=
ogram tier and add-ons; Agent 2b (<code>WriteNarrative</code>) produces pat=
ient-facing communication script; both run concurrently</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"5815b18f-3e56-4033-b99d-9080f7131920" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a584902b91ba">Either agent can fail independently; per-field=
 fallback applied</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"c357c9c1-f038-4056-bfc4-fd48286ef441">
<td data-local-id=3D"b4ad8aae-7a26-4624-94cc-dfa36a8313a0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"3b815503c3b8"><strong>Phase 4 =E2=80=94 Safety Validation + =
Audit + Response</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"73f68ebb-f132-42f4-a2c7-8ea8c5de9c7a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"706e17d8e8cd"><code>SafetyRuleValidator</code> filters gende=
r/age/contraindication-ineligible add-ons; audit log written synchronously;=
 response delivered to caller</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"4caa92c3-d498-4c85-bba0-df4714055ef1" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"87867f16425f">Frontend resolves patient identity from <code>=
patient_id</code> at display time</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"db8c3e8e1c09" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.1.3WorkflowDiagram">7.1.3 Workflow Diagram</h3>
<div>
We don't have a way to export this macro.
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-1713573490" class=3D"expand-container">
<div id=3D"expander-control-1713573490" class=3D"expand-control">
