<h3 local-id=3D"33b04540cfa3" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.1.4GracefulDegradation">7.1.4 Graceful Degradation</=
h3>
<p local-id=3D"fa8972fbea7f">The pipeline is designed to always produce a r=
ecommendation. Failures are handled at the coarsest applicable boundary:</p=
>
<ul local-id=3D"1aeca0a9-0bff-48c9-be8e-98527cdf1061">
<li local-id=3D"05959ebf-729e-4a2a-aa75-c3bff389debb">
<p local-id=3D"f728af840a35"><strong>Agent 1 failure</strong> =E2=86=92 ful=
l rule-based output; AI chain bypassed entirely</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"443abe3c-8626-4038-9f87-f4d5675b2d88">
<p local-id=3D"bd3225f583e0"><strong>Agent 2a (</strong><code>MatchPolicy</=
code><strong>) failure only</strong> =E2=86=92 rule-based tier applied; sig=
nal-matched add-ons substituted; <code>review_required: true</code></p></li=
>
<li local-id=3D"731333a5-68ac-4bad-bb79-adb2b8b9d6b5">
<p local-id=3D"5c26833fffbd"><strong>Agent 2b (</strong><code>WriteNarrativ=
e</code><strong>) failure only</strong> =E2=86=92 narrative constructed fro=
m Agent 1 clinical summary bullets</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b97b4cae-e173-4ac2-80d9-9df3730a4138">
<p local-id=3D"c515a081a220"><strong>Both Agent 2a and 2b failure</strong> =
=E2=86=92 full rule-based output</p></li>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"60b45563d9c9">In degraded states where the AI tier is unavai=
lable (Agent 1 failure, Agent 2a failure, or both Agent 2a and 2b failure),=
 <code>recommendation_source</code> is set to <code>"RuleBased"</code> and =
<code>review_required</code> is set to <code>true</code>, signalling to the=
 clinical UI that human review is required before acting on the recommendat=
ion. When only Agent 2b fails, the AI-selected tier and add-ons are retaine=
d and <code>recommendation_source</code> remains <code>"AI"</code> =E2=80=
=94 only the patient-facing narrative is degraded.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"42d18c1fc34e" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.2ModelContextProtocol(MCP)Middleware(SecureContextRe=
trieval)">7.2 Model Context Protocol (MCP) Middleware (Secure Context Retri=
eval)</h2>
<p local-id=3D"0b7672a67d58"></p>
<p local-id=3D"58c75765eed9">The Model Context Protocol (MCP) middleware la=
yer sits between the clinical data platform and the AI inference pipeline. =
It exposes a standardised set of read-only tool interfaces that the AI agen=
ts use to retrieve structured patient context on demand. This section defin=
es the <strong>MCP =E2=86=92 AI interface</strong>: the tools, the clinical=
 data they expose, and how each is consumed.</p>
<blockquote local-id=3D"204248c4e115">
<p local-id=3D"bdd56f9ac475"><em>Note: The MCP Server combines tool-serving=
 and data-access responsibilities in a single service. This is a deliberate=
 design choice for operational simplicity at the projected Year 1 scale (30=
 concurrent users). The MCP does not perform authorization itself =E2=80=94=
 it delegates all access control decisions to the SMART on FHIR Authorizati=
on Server by forwarding the calling user's scoped token on every database q=
uery. The MCP's database credentials are restricted to </em><code>SELECT</c=
ode><em>-only on </em><code>masked_clinical_fhir</code><em> and </em><code>=
trending</code><em> schemas, limiting blast radius. If the system scales be=
yond Year 2 projections, the data-access layer can be extracted into a sepa=
rate service behind the MCP without changing the tool interface contract.</=
em></p>
</blockquote>
<p local-id=3D"545641e02645"><strong>Data Platform Specifications:</strong>=
</p>
<ul local-id=3D"0de65c6e3c18">
<li local-id=3D"70d4352ce86e">
<p local-id=3D"f60b4493cdf1"><strong>Datastore Technology:</strong> Tools r=
etrieving raw clinical records (<code>get_hard_constraints</code>, <code>ge=
t_patient_event_timeline</code>, <code>get_program_ruleset</code>) query th=
e <strong>Silver Layer</strong> (Masked FHIR Store via PostgreSQL/AWS Healt=
hLake). Analytical tools (<code>get_clinical_signals</code>, <code>get_biom=
arker_trends</code>) query the <strong>Gold Layer</strong> (Lakehouse via C=
lickHouse/Amazon Redshift) for pre-computed trends and metrics.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"00f3554a62d6">
<p local-id=3D"e7f9457796c8"><strong>Ingestion Pipeline:</strong> Event-dri=
ven architecture using CDC (Debezium/AWS DMS) from IQVIA/EMR, feeding throu=
gh an event bus (Kafka/MSK) into Bronze storage, followed by standardizatio=
n, PII masking (Silver), and metric aggregation (Gold).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"31bf4659da5c">
<p local-id=3D"eb10d9c73ac8"><strong>Refresh Cadence:</strong> Near real-ti=
me (&lt;100ms latency) for continuous CDC streams; micro-batch updates for =
complex Gold layer trends. Legacy/bulk imports via nightly batch (4-hour wi=
ndow).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"35452c8ce2dd">
<p local-id=3D"f4d51c5ff121"><strong>Availability SLAs:</strong> 99.9% syst=
em uptime via Multi-AZ deployment. Sub-500ms latency for FHIR queries (Silv=
er) and sub-200ms latency for analytics queries (Gold).</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"750479cc1e88" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.2.1ToolInterface">7.2.1 Tool Interface</h3>
<p local-id=3D"ac12a445672f">The MCP server exposes five read-only tools, e=
ach scoped to a single patient identified by <code>patient_token</code>. Fo=
ur tools feed the AI inference pipeline; one feeds the clinical UI directly=
 and is never sent to an LLM.</p>
