<h4 local-id=3D"60f9bdceafd8" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-SeasonalPriorityEscalation"><strong>Seasonal Priority =
Escalation</strong></h4>
<p local-id=3D"e21c16a441c4">A system-level seasonal context (computed from=
 the current calendar date; no patient data required) is injected into the =
<code>get_program_ruleset</code> response at query time. The AI uses this t=
o escalate vaccination urgency during peak disease periods (Thailand season=
s: Cool Nov=E2=80=93Feb, Hot Mar=E2=80=93Jun, Rainy Jul=E2=80=93Oct).</p>
<p local-id=3D"825178ab96cc">For example: Influenza vaccination gaps escala=
te to Orange priority during Rainy season; seasonal timing guidance is incl=
uded in <code>communication_script.next_steps</code>.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"eb91d972ed20" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.3.3SafetyValidationChecks">7.3.3 Safety Validation C=
hecks</h3>
<p local-id=3D"80bad440f927">After AI-driven add-on selection, <code>Safety=
RuleValidator</code> applies four deterministic checks against each recomme=
nded item:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"bcfde8d2-fe69-41fb-af39-22d2667fc6ed">
<li local-id=3D"5864476f-7019-4d47-9fd2-b387cf73f6da">
<p local-id=3D"624e65216605"><strong>Item validity</strong> =E2=80=94 item =
ID must exist in the current add-on library</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"50586096-d9a7-4532-94d3-6715b73d0d39">
<p local-id=3D"973d05213781"><strong>Gender constraint</strong> =E2=80=94 a=
dd-ons with a gender restriction are removed if the patient does not match<=
/p></li>
<li local-id=3D"a06e8804-9c52-4347-be8c-d29b920ad1f2">
<p local-id=3D"d65400f4e5df"><strong>Age bounds</strong> =E2=80=94 add-ons =
with a minimum or maximum age requirement are removed if the patient is out=
side the eligible range</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9731ef44-70b8-4a28-ae33-5e7ee9f57b49">
<p local-id=3D"0d9b48f0fced"><strong>Contraindication signals</strong> =E2=
=80=94 add-ons that define contraindication signals are removed if any of t=
hose signals are active for the patient</p></li>
</ol>
<p local-id=3D"9f938a2679c0">Removed items do not appear in the final recom=
mendation. Each removal is recorded as a <code>safety_conflict_event</code>=
 with the item ID and violation reason, captured in the <code>What</code> d=
imension of the audit log.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"552f92461db8" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.3.4FallbackChain">7.3.4 Fallback Chain</h3>
<p local-id=3D"dfe0cc0f8b8e">If AI components are unavailable, the recommen=
dation engine degrades in steps, always producing a usable output:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1057" data-layout=3D"center" data-local-id=3D"f7=
38c75f-aac6-4726-a996-23df7a7c255e" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 424.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 632.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"a229906e-4de5-422b-87a6-1e6b9522d2b6">
<th data-local-id=3D"759c289d-083e-4232-a61b-3580ce7ddfe3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"ace5d5a24b9a">Failure Scenario</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"d30a300b-4dff-4602-82d0-495ce369843d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"0f3d8cafb971">Output</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"d03a10a0-d8c0-47df-a36f-23dc4f660c86">
<td data-local-id=3D"a8a8d927-d17a-4ffe-b021-7fc3ab058c53" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"97e1b9c17dc4">Agent 1 (<code>AnalyzeClinicalRisks</code>) fa=
ils</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"58338ab4-535a-4dae-821f-ba1352c31cc2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8cc78f314c1f">Full rule-based recommendation; AI pipeline by=
passed</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"f76e1902-ab44-46c4-abc0-8eeebad06089">
<td data-local-id=3D"7629ee78-c145-4803-afa7-6702858c97de" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"0bbd56a9c8db">Agent 2a (<code>MatchPolicy</code>) fails, Age=
nt 2b succeeds</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"0eeefa73-0952-4e7d-925a-41e52fdcb790" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"bc5ead97084d">Rule-based tier applied; signal-matched add-on=
s used; <code>review_required: true</code></p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"061b0860-08c7-45b4-b05b-81ffdd6ea038">
<td data-local-id=3D"26db745f-fdb1-4799-8580-cff06969f126" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f6e7418440d5">Agent 2b (<code>WriteNarrative</code>) fails, =
Agent 2a succeeds</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"434cbe2a-0c5b-410e-983f-a8508d3b9194" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ffd7ce933116">Narrative constructed from Agent 1 clinical su=
mmary bullets</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ad63779a-f605-4b11-ba9c-1a837d566081">
<td data-local-id=3D"410425ae-6e88-45d3-ab76-f7b4a8b6dd85" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"68eed89068d1">Both Agent 2a and 2b fail</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"ebf5b11a-83e0-46fa-84a0-5a3d152a70db" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"312122aba22d">Full rule-based recommendation; <code>review_r=
equired: true</code></p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<p local-id=3D"45ac8099dc73">In degraded states where the AI tier is unavai=
lable (Agent 1 failure, Agent 2a failure, or both Agent 2a and 2b failure),=
 <code>recommendation_source</code> is set to <code>"RuleBased"</code> and =
<code>review_required</code> is set to <code>true</code>. When only Agent 2=
b fails, the AI-selected tier and add-ons are retained and <code>recommenda=
tion_source</code> remains <code>"AI"</code> =E2=80=94 only the patient-fac=
ing narrative is degraded.</p>
<h2 local-id=3D"4eb8f618c50c" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.4CentralAIGateway">7.4 Central AI Gateway</h2>
<p local-id=3D"59b6e4fd5376">The Central AI Gateway is a dedicated routing =
and abstraction layer that sits between the clinical application and all ex=
ternal LLM providers. Its purpose is to ensure that the clinical agent pipe=
line has no direct dependency on any specific AI provider =E2=80=94 model s=
election, fallback behaviour, timeout enforcement, and credential managemen=
t are all handled at the gateway layer, invisible to the application code a=
bove it.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"beb58617181c" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.4.1Responsibilities">7.4.1 Responsibilities</h3>
<p local-id=3D"0a4c7177e3bc"><strong>Provider abstraction.</strong> Clinica=
l agents issue inference requests through a single, stable interface. The u=
nderlying model =E2=80=94 whether from a cloud AI lab, an open-source deplo=
yment, or an on-premise server =E2=80=94 is resolved at runtime by the gate=
way. No provider-specific client code exists in the application layer.</p>
<p local-id=3D"84acc15b3647"><strong>Automatic fallback chain.</strong> The=
 gateway maintains an ordered list of model candidates. If the configured p=
rimary model is unavailable, times out, or returns an unrecoverable error, =
the gateway automatically retries with the next candidate in the chain. Thi=
s process is transparent to the clinical agent =E2=80=94 the agent receives=
 a valid response or a clean failure, never a partially-handled provider er=
ror.</p>
<p local-id=3D"20bff8ca1d45"><strong>Per-call timeout enforcement.</strong>=
 Every inference call is subject to a maximum wall-clock timeout, configure=
d at the gateway level. This bounds worst-case latency regardless of provid=
er behaviour and prevents a slow or unresponsive model from blocking the re=
commendation pipeline.</p>
<p local-id=3D"860abe79d00a"><strong>Credential isolation.</strong> Provide=
r API keys are managed via environment configuration and are never referenc=
ed in application code. Rotating credentials or changing providers requires=
 no code change.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9a8b79af0b19"><strong>Structured output contract.</strong> T=
he gateway enforces that every model response conforms to the typed output =
schema expected by the calling agent. Raw unstructured text never reaches t=
he clinical logic layer =E2=80=94 schema validation failures are handled at=
 the gateway boundary, not scattered through the application.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"11a9838e674f" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.4.2RelationshiptoClinicalAgents">7.4.2 Relationship =
to Clinical Agents</h3>
<p local-id=3D"1a720a0bf0f5">All three clinical agents =E2=80=94 <code>Anal=
yzeClinicalRisks</code>, <code>MatchPolicy</code>, and <code>WriteNarrative=
</code> =E2=80=94 route their inference calls through the gateway. They are=
 authored against the typed contract; the gateway resolves which model fulf=
ils it at runtime. This separation allows the active model to be changed wi=
thout touching any agent definition.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"20db37dcbe12" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.4.3ExplainableAI(XAI)&amp;ConfidenceScoringGeneratio=
n">7.4.3 Explainable AI (XAI) &amp; Confidence Scoring Generation</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a6664591ee5d">Every recommendation produced by the AI pipeli=
ne includes a structured explanation and a system-computed confidence score=
. These are designed to support physician judgement =E2=80=94 not replace i=
t =E2=80=94 by making the AI's clinical reasoning transparent and quantifia=
ble.</p>
<h4 local-id=3D"4b4900755d36" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-ReasoningTrace">Reasoning Trace</h4>
<p local-id=3D"f7a32081c15c">The reasoning trace is assembled from two sour=
ces within the AI pipeline:</p>
<ul local-id=3D"1372c26a-c13e-4e88-a623-6707914ff464">
<li local-id=3D"20f90e29-b29e-4796-979b-2845fb82ee3d">
<p local-id=3D"db54a8707289"><strong>Clinical risk profile bullets</strong>=
 =E2=80=94 produced by Agent 1 (<code>AnalyzeClinicalRisks</code>): a struc=
tured set of identified risk factors, severity classifications, and contrai=
ndication flags derived from the patient's clinical signals</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f5ebd04f-0b37-48fd-b136-ee64ceb2efc5">
<p local-id=3D"e879f3a475c2"><strong>Policy reasoning</strong> =E2=80=94 pr=
oduced by Agent 2a (<code>MatchPolicy</code>): the AI's written justificati=
on for the selected tier and add-on items, including a mandatory deviation =
justification if the AI overrides the rule-computed preliminary tier</p></l=
i>
</ul>
<p local-id=3D"e36beaf1ce68">These two outputs are combined into the <code>=
reasoning_trace</code> field exposed in the API response, giving the physic=
ian a readable account of why a specific recommendation was generated.</p>
<h4 local-id=3D"8730918bdafe" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-ConfidenceScore">Confidence Score</h4>
<p local-id=3D"68225f20ac01">The confidence score is computed deterministic=
ally by the system after AI inference =E2=80=94 it is not a self-reported p=
robability from the LLM. This design prevents the model from producing arti=
ficially high confidence values and ensures the score reflects the actual c=
ompleteness of the available clinical data.</p>
<p local-id=3D"ee156742010c">The formula:</p>
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">confide=
nce_score =3D 0.4 =C3=97 signal_coverage + 0.4 =C3=97 data_completeness + 0=
.2 =C3=97 rule_agreement</pre>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1048" data-layout=3D"center" data-local-id=3D"17=
49e968-c912-47d5-97b0-61a28bea9479" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 194.0px;">
