<p local-id=3D"9d52261177ed">All XAI fields =E2=80=94 the reasoning trace, =
confidence score, confidence tier, and communication script =E2=80=94 are i=
ncluded in the API response and available to the clinical UI for physician =
display.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"e7c57ccf8bc7" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-7.4.4PluggableLLMConfigurationManagement">7.4.4 Plugga=
ble LLM Configuration Management</h3>
<p local-id=3D"f4492a5d0e7d">The AI gateway is designed to be fully provide=
r-agnostic. The active model is a <strong>configuration value</strong>, not=
 a code dependency. Switching from one model to another =E2=80=94 whether a=
cross providers, model sizes, or deployment modes =E2=80=94 requires a sing=
le configuration update and a service restart. No application code changes,=
 no redeployment, and no schema migration are needed.</p>
<h4 local-id=3D"b975a4ee138c" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-ZeroVendorLock-In">Zero Vendor Lock-In</h4>
<p local-id=3D"1f92ee420227">This architecture was a deliberate design choi=
ce to protect the project against the rapid pace of change in the AI model =
landscape. As newer, more capable models become available from different pr=
oviders, the hospital is free to adopt them immediately. Similarly, if cost=
, data sovereignty, or regulatory requirements shift =E2=80=94 such as a ne=
ed to move from cloud inference to fully on-premise =E2=80=94 the transitio=
n can be made at the configuration layer without touching any clinical logi=
c.</p>
