</div>
<p local-id=3D"b7bf576ae0a2">Each container has its own <code>Dockerfile</c=
ode>, health check, resource limits, and can be scaled, replaced, or upgrad=
ed independently without affecting other services =E2=80=94 directly satisf=
ying TOR =C2=A74.3's "Plug/Unplug" requirement.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"6f9c1603241d" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-8.1.6Non-BlockingUXPattern(TOR=C2=A76.3)">8.1.6 Non-Bl=
ocking UX Pattern (TOR =C2=A76.3)</h3>
<p local-id=3D"358b5d04bb74">The TOR mandates that the UI must be <strong>n=
on-blocking</strong> =E2=80=94 the interface should never freeze while wait=
ing for AI recommendation results. The React architecture achieves this thr=
ough:</p>
<ol start=3D"1" local-id=3D"7a7eab43-e895-4473-92f0-24cfe0b82e6b">
<li local-id=3D"d2fcd1dc-f966-4ec3-81f2-565c7120614f">
<p local-id=3D"0117e6d3575a"><strong>Asynchronous Data Fetching:</strong> A=
ll API calls are made via React Query's <code>useQuery</code> / <code>useMu=
tation</code> hooks, which run in the background. The UI renders immediatel=
y with a skeleton/shimmer loading state.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b84ee3d6-0ddd-4a75-879c-1a61b4e48bf2">
<p local-id=3D"191edf96fd7d"><strong>Progressive Rendering:</strong> The In=
dividual Summary screen loads in stages =E2=80=94 patient demographics and =
historical data (from the fast FHIR DB read) render first, while the AI rec=
ommendation (which may take up to 10 seconds) loads asynchronously and slot=
s into the page once available.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"9cc2f2c9-aa8b-4f54-bcaa-2efb71e7e9dc">
<p local-id=3D"701c6e963525"><strong>Optimistic UI for Admin Actions:</stro=
ng> Mapping Tool and Master Data changes appear instantly in the UI while t=
he backend processes the request, with automatic rollback if the server rej=
ects the change.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"1c4fed5c-a420-4b9d-b643-a33f854f08b4">
<p local-id=3D"54ba2ec0d400"><strong>WebSocket/SSE for Real-Time Feeds:</st=
rong> The Access Monitoring Dashboard receives live updates via persistent =
connections rather than polling, eliminating unnecessary re-renders and net=
work overhead.</p></li>
</ol>
<h2 local-id=3D"eb9ac38f68fe" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-8.2BusinessIntelligence&amp;ConversionDashboard(TOR=C2=
=A77)">8.2 <span class=3D"inline-comment-marker" data-ref=3D"1acd391c-521a-=
425b-bde7-45acb7f79c57">Business Intelligence &amp; Conversion Dashboard (T=
OR =C2=A77)</span></h2>
<p local-id=3D"97de0b4ee946">The TOR (=C2=A77) requires a Business Intellig=
ence layer that tracks whether AI-generated health checkup recommendations =
actually convert into purchased services, and provides an executive-level p=
erformance view. This introduces a new stakeholder group =E2=80=94 <strong>=
Management / Executives</strong> =E2=80=94 alongside Healthcare Providers a=
nd DPO/Admin.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"da28521b1aca" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-8.2.1Stakeholders&amp;AccessControl">8.2.1 Stakeholder=
s &amp; Access Control</h3>
<p local-id=3D"5b2590060e44">The <strong>Healthcare Provider</strong> role =
encompasses the full patient consultation workflow =E2=80=94 from generatin=
g AI recommendations, to presenting and explaining the checkup plan to the =
patient, to capturing the patient's acceptance or refusal. There is no sepa=
rate "Sales" role; the provider handles both clinical and consultative resp=
onsibilities.</p>
