<h1 local-id=3D"c87c2780389a" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-9.Deployment&amp;OperationalArchitecture"><strong>9. D=
eployment &amp; Operational Architecture</strong></h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"2a008305838e" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-9.1On-PremiseDeploymentStrategy">9.1 On-Premise Deploy=
ment Strategy</h2>
<p local-id=3D"5d3c7033aa9e">The Smart Health Checkup Recommendation Dashbo=
ard is deployed entirely <strong>on-premise</strong> within Navavej Hospita=
l's own data center. This decision is driven by the strict data residency r=
equirements of PDPA, the hospital's preference for full infrastructure owne=
rship, and the elimination of recurring cloud compute costs. All system com=
ponents run as <strong>Docker containers</strong> orchestrated by Docker Co=
mpose on hospital-managed servers, using exclusively open-source software (=
OSS) with no proprietary cloud service dependencies.</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"a2dd799b546c" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-9.1.1PhysicalInfrastructure&amp;HardwareSizing">9.1.1 =
Physical Infrastructure &amp; Hardware Sizing</h3>
<p local-id=3D"8c9fbc2a188d">The system requires a minimum of two physical =
servers (or VMs) to satisfy basic high-availability and separation-of-conce=
rn requirements:</p>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1048" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"a2b437e3-abab-4609-b24d-8f8c1e47249f" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 262.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 253.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 270.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 262.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"d9e25e84-7cd4-403c-865b-2890aaf59652">
<th data-local-id=3D"af3313fc-a957-44b4-bf3c-9fd566929cc1" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"22e9891e8275">Server Role</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"f07061a8-ec8a-4f9b-a538-f3a919e15b8d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"e8e070259696">Purpose</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"91fb2284-40de-45cd-be7e-0a520cfea4a4" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"5191c01bfe6e">Recommended Minimum Spec</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"6344014b-ca22-48c5-825c-87c2d7068eda" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"e3b97ddd9aa3">Containers Hosted</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"291a1895-e1c6-4e44-8ad5-ad895ab9efe1">
<td data-local-id=3D"bf3052ea-9f63-439b-9e3e-4cd47cd545a3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"13bddac1791d"><strong>Application Server</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"030d565d-8ed0-4d9b-addf-ab6d43577be8" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7e3d471853b2">Runs all application-tier containers</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c47792b0-8525-4327-8c6e-4ae7b44cf24c" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"75203647e6b9">16 vCPU, 32 GB RAM, 200 GB SSD</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"47c1bcad-63cc-4745-ac54-7f049158ccfd" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1a77776f426e"><code>frontend</code>, <code>backend-api</code=
>, <code>mcp-server</code>, <code>ai-gateway</code>, <code>auth-server</cod=
e>, <code>reverse-proxy</code></p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"bae97bb4-0c88-4fb9-8414-467c421043c2">
<td data-local-id=3D"ff7f44a4-1409-4992-a20a-6953fb97dd11" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6dd18cfaa200"><strong>Database Server</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"1f80032e-438a-45a9-bc26-79b599fe4832" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9ce13f7a04a9">Runs all database and storage containers</p></=
td>
<td data-local-id=3D"169236ac-889a-4d5e-8eeb-26fc1fd13960" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"6dbe2d393da4">8 vCPU, 32 GB RAM, 1 TB SSD (RAID-10)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"031df6f8-2f54-46f3-abe1-918dc8cbefb6" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"7278033c1f46"><code>fhir-db</code>, <code>trending-db</code>=
, <code>audit-db</code></p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<blockquote local-id=3D"bf1a45c1-cf0d-42dc-b01d-7a53d2d0e9e4">
<p local-id=3D"647594fce5fc"><strong>Scaling Note:</strong> For Year 1 oper=
ations (estimated &lt; 50 concurrent users, &lt; 10,000 patient records act=
ively queried per day), a 2 server setup is sufficient. As patient volume g=
rows (Year 2=E2=80=933), horizontal scaling can be achieved by migrating fr=
om Docker Compose to a lightweight Kubernetes distribution (e.g., <strong>K=
3s</strong>, open-source) or by adding replicated Application Servers behin=
d a load balancer.</p>
</blockquote>
<p local-id=3D"bf0a90fa4892"><strong>Network Prerequisites</strong></p>
<ul local-id=3D"1e074991-622b-426b-8e4c-378a8ec397ac">
<li local-id=3D"4a258a8d-cc95-423a-beda-5036abcaee11">
<p local-id=3D"0c141a1ed497">Both servers must reside on the same private n=
etwork (VLAN) with low-latency connectivity (&lt; 1 ms).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"64c4872a-5876-4c57-bc61-2e53162f5b68">
<p local-id=3D"df08a5c1320d">The Application Server requires outbound HTTPS=
 access (port 443) to external AI provider APIs (OpenAI, Anthropic) =E2=80=
=94 unless using a local LLM exclusively.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"6f51488a-a709-4256-a4fb-44affc763686">
<p local-id=3D"303b75b2e553">The Database Server should have <strong>no dir=
ect outbound internet access</strong> =E2=80=94 all external communication =
is proxied through the Application Server.</p></li>
</ul>
<h3 local-id=3D"0416ba616138" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-9.1.2DockerComposeServiceArchitecture">9.1.2 Docker Co=
mpose Service Architecture</h3>
<p local-id=3D"a3f5cd44f2f4">All services are defined in a single <code>doc=
ker-compose.yml</code> and managed as a unified stack. Each service runs in=
 its own container with explicit resource limits, health checks, and restar=
t policies.</p>
<p local-id=3D"9410bd9d6c5a"><strong>Docker Compose Service Definitions</st=
rong></p>
<div id=3D"expander-395287773" class=3D"expand-container">
<div id=3D"expander-control-395287773" class=3D"expand-control">
<span class=3D"expand-control-icon"><img style=3D"vertical-align:middle;" c=
lass=3D"expand-control-image" src=3D"12d6790ad24896d77c6798d608975ef510283c=
c49b55e6f0ab90f21b044efffb" width=3D"16" height=3D"16"></span><span class=
=3D"expand-control-text">mermaid</span>
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-content-395287773" class=3D"expand-content">
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">flowcha=
rt LR
    subgraph HospitalLAN ["Hospital Internal Network (LAN)"]
        Browser["=F0=9F=A7=91=E2=80=8D=E2=9A=95=EF=B8=8F Healthcare Provide=
r's Browser"]
        Admin["=F0=9F=9B=A1=EF=B8=8F DPO Browser"]
        HIS["=F0=9F=8F=A2 Navavej HIS (IQVIA)"]
    end

    subgraph DockerNetwork ["Docker Internal Network (172.x.x.x)"]
        Proxy["Nginx :443&lt;br&gt;(Only Exposed Port)"]
        Services["All Application&lt;br&gt;Containers"]
        DBs["All Database&lt;br&gt;Containers"]
    end

    subgraph External ["External (Outbound Only)"]
        AI_APIs["AI Provider APIs&lt;br&gt;(OpenAI / Anthropic)"]
    end

    Browser --&gt;|HTTPS :443| Proxy
    Admin --&gt;|HTTPS :443| Proxy
    HIS --&gt;|"CDC Sync (internal)"| Services
    Proxy --&gt; Services
    Services --&gt; DBs
    Services --&gt;|HTTPS :443 outbound| AI_APIs</pre>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
