<h3 local-id=3D"d592c1771095" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-9.3.2RecoveryProcedures">9.3.2 Recovery Procedures</h3=
>
<div class=3D"table-wrap">
<table data-table-width=3D"1011" data-layout=3D"align-start" data-local-id=
=3D"c9f74064-9fd5-4ef0-bb02-1d8c115d1439" class=3D"confluenceTable">
<colgroup>
<col style=3D"width: 240.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 285.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 228.0px;">
<col style=3D"width: 252.0px;">
</colgroup>
<tbody>
<tr data-local-id=3D"c9377f85-e460-44cd-b8f2-231139f2ed8b">
<th data-local-id=3D"1614c32a-c2be-4f59-82ed-fc172a862b8e" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"37c7a2628866">Scenario</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"32f2c51f-0f6e-4509-9ae7-00b30553ccd3" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"2c10c1b082e5">RTO (Recovery Time Objective)</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"19399c60-6548-4c7c-bb39-f3dafdecf723" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"188827417fa5">RPO (Recovery Point Objective)</p></th>
<th data-local-id=3D"859738af-0c2a-4ff1-b358-febaeb44a45a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTh">
<p local-id=3D"fbc0d0fa489a">Procedure</p></th>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"6e331e28-0135-4aad-8042-6b8a68ec89c2">
<td data-local-id=3D"f36dbf6a-cd03-4b29-aaa2-718840dc8877" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9cabe1d3538f"><strong>Single container crash</strong></p></t=
d>
<td data-local-id=3D"35ccb3a9-5f9f-4d08-b3df-b9e19a7e17ef" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"53deecf51bad">&lt; 1 minute</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"3eaabd7f-1efb-4e41-aa60-6e7ff56b4734" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9a892250e5c5">Zero data loss</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"30145976-502f-46a9-86f4-fa2b3fd1d92d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1c30093acf0b">Docker <code>restart: always</code> policy aut=
o-recovers the container.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"0c01daaa-f0c9-4c57-b45e-75941251c3e6">
<td data-local-id=3D"9c6bd231-6007-4051-8379-7706ee9fcbaf" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b088d77fb707"><strong>Application Server failure</strong></p=
></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"21c66466-8d13-462a-be53-f1e1c4516225" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b2be4418e554">&lt; 1 hour</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"05038bc2-25d1-4e49-9d9b-23af963be110" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ac122ec0486b">Zero data loss</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"33054642-c62f-40e9-a4a4-2a0454e1911f" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a5c78e9c7dfe">Re-deploy <code>docker-compose up -d</code> on=
 a standby server using the same images and configuration from Git. Databas=
e is on a separate server and unaffected.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"3367a05d-22be-48e1-b98c-ce46393e5b73">
<td data-local-id=3D"b484c890-8984-45f5-90fa-3a49ec6ef835" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9b8b77788b93"><strong>Database Server failure</strong></p></=
td>
<td data-local-id=3D"28c3e565-504e-4fa4-9914-89aaa93067f4" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"613b5f94889d">&lt; 4 hours</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"a8ed4c57-7fb9-42ce-acb4-f4dae75e45ea" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b94630e8ed5f">&lt; 24 hours (daily backup) or &lt; 5 minutes=
 (WAL recovery)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"384b0d7c-1668-4fb5-9daf-1031f5bb400d" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"39baffdbf91c">Restore from <code>pgBackRest</code> backup to=
 a replacement server. Replay WAL logs for point-in-time recovery.</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"4d02bd01-cbec-47e9-aac5-ef886f2b9c24">
<td data-local-id=3D"9f7435d9-0c38-488e-9128-9748ff7566b0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"670ba6ba274f"><strong>Full site disaster</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c018a118-51a6-4dad-9f45-79768f566660" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"725a81c88a95">&lt; 8 hours</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"2aa6846c-b63c-44d6-9c80-4cfae73935be" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"094fa37416f4">&lt; 1 week (offsite backup)</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"ef353b0f-fdf0-4503-8d07-e535b77cff75" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"47ed57b5c32b">Provision new servers, restore from offsite en=
crypted backup, re-deploy all containers.</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"6370abcff66e" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-9.3.3DataIntegrity&amp;Immutability">9.3.3 Data Integr=
ity &amp; Immutability</h3>
<ul local-id=3D"0d572508-d5fb-401d-a79e-42db0ca087a4">
<li local-id=3D"fbaa909b-9c86-4332-b8c6-2c257ebc3bad">
<p local-id=3D"d450de072d71"><strong>Audit Log Immutability:</strong> The <=
code>audit-db</code> PostgreSQL instance enforces immutability through data=
base-level triggers that prevent <code>UPDATE</code> and <code>DELETE</code=
> operations on audit tables. The database user for the <code>backend-api</=
code> service has only <code>INSERT</code> and <code>SELECT</code> privileg=
es on audit tables =E2=80=94 no <code>UPDATE</code>, <code>DELETE</code>, o=
r <code>TRUNCATE</code>.</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"b9d177bb-05bd-4ba9-a3a9-f39f1fefbcd7">
<p local-id=3D"cf309453441c"><strong>FHIR Record Integrity:</strong> The <c=
ode>clinical_fhir</code> schema uses append-only patterns for clinical reco=
rds. Historical records are never modified; corrections are stored as new F=
HIR resources with references to the original (per FHIR versioning semantic=
s).</p></li>
<li local-id=3D"f4370b75-29cc-49c4-8591-384155a0476b">
<p local-id=3D"090ad6c73699"><strong>Backup Verification:</strong> Automate=
d weekly test restores are executed against a temporary PostgreSQL instance=
 to verify backup integrity. Results are logged and surfaced on the System =
Health Grafana dashboard.</p></li>
</ul>
<h1 local-id=3D"06a4d830adbf" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-10.QualityAssurance&amp;Non-FunctionalRequirements(NFR=
s)"><strong>10. Quality Assurance &amp; Non-Functional Requirements (NFRs)<=
/strong></h1>
<h2 local-id=3D"4a593103213e" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-10.1PerformanceMetrics&amp;SLAs">10.1 Performance Metr=
ics &amp; SLAs</h2>
<p local-id=3D"a4d5cf777775">The TOR (=C2=A76.3) defines two distinct perfo=
rmance tiers based on whether the patient's data has already been ingested =
and pre-processed (existing customer) or requires first-time extraction fro=
m the HIS (new customer). The system is designed to meet both tiers through=
 the architectural decisions described in prior sections =E2=80=94 namely p=
re-masked data (=C2=A76.2), pre-computed trending features (=C2=A74.3.3), a=
nd non-blocking progressive UI rendering (=C2=A78.1.6).</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"1c06ba66bbc0" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-10.1.1LatencySLATargets">10.1.1 Latency SLA Targets</h=
3>
