<h2 local-id=3D"ad8475f05d14" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-10.4Safety&quot;Fallback&quot;Rules">10.4 Safety "Fall=
back" Rules</h2>
<p local-id=3D"098fac911b1d">The TOR (=C2=A76.2) requires that the system i=
nclude configurable Safety Rules and a Safety Fallback mechanism to ensure =
that AI recommendations never compromise patient safety. The Hybrid Recomme=
ndation Engine (=C2=A73.3, item 5) implements this through a <strong>three-=
layer safety architecture</strong>:</p>
<h3 local-id=3D"81165e4d18dd" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-10.4.1Three-LayerSafetyArchitecture">10.4.1 Three-Laye=
r Safety Architecture</h3>
<div>
We don't have a way to export this macro.
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-1932460072" class=3D"expand-container">
<div id=3D"expander-control-1932460072" class=3D"expand-control">
<span class=3D"expand-control-icon"><img style=3D"vertical-align:middle;" c=
lass=3D"expand-control-image" src=3D"12d6790ad24896d77c6798d608975ef510283c=
c49b55e6f0ab90f21b044efffb" width=3D"16" height=3D"16"></span><span class=
=3D"expand-control-text">mermaid</span>
</div>
<div id=3D"expander-content-1932460072" class=3D"expand-content">
<div class=3D"code panel pdl" style=3D"border-width: 1px;">
<div class=3D"codeContent panelContent pdl">
<pre class=3D"syntaxhighlighter-pre" data-syntaxhighlighter-params=3D"brush=
: java; gutter: false; theme: Confluence" data-theme=3D"Confluence">flowcha=
rt TD
    Request["Patient context received&lt;br&gt;by Hybrid Engine"] --&gt; Pr=
eRules

    subgraph Layer1 ["Layer 1: Pre-AI Safety Rules"]
        PreRules["Apply deterministic&lt;br&gt;safety constraints BEFORE&lt=
;br&gt;sending to AI"]
        PreRules --&gt; Check1{"Gender-specific&lt;br&gt;screening limits?"=
}
        Check1 --&gt;|"=E2=9D=8C Mammogram for male"| Block1["Block &amp; l=
og&lt;br&gt;rule violation"]
        Check1 --&gt;|"=E2=9C=85 OK"| Check2{"Age-range&lt;br&gt;limits?"}
        Check2 --&gt;|"=E2=9D=8C Under minimum age"| Block2["Block &amp; lo=
g&lt;br&gt;rule violation"]
        Check2 --&gt;|"=E2=9C=85 OK"| SendAI["Send to AI Gateway"]
    end

    SendAI --&gt; AIInference["=F0=9F=A4=96 Gemini 1.5 Pro&lt;br&gt;AI Infe=
rence"]

    subgraph Layer2 ["Layer 2: Post-AI Safety Validation"]
        AIInference --&gt; PostRules["Validate AI output&lt;br&gt;against A=
LL safety rules"]
        PostRules --&gt; Conflict{"AI recommendation&lt;br&gt;conflicts wit=
h&lt;br&gt;Safety Rule?"}
        Conflict --&gt;|"YES"| Revoke["=E2=9B=94 REVOKE conflicting&lt;br&g=
t;recommendation items"]
        Conflict --&gt;|"NO"| Pass["=E2=9C=85 Pass through"]
    end

    subgraph Layer3 ["Layer 3: AI Failure Fallback"]
        Revoke --&gt; Fallback
        AIInference --&gt;|"Timeout / Error / Crash"| Fallback["=F0=9F=9B=
=A1=EF=B8=8F Safety Fallback:&lt;br&gt;Use Rule-Based Only&lt;br&gt;(no AI)=
"]
        Fallback --&gt; RuleOnly["Generate recommendation&lt;br&gt;using de=
terministic rules&lt;br&gt;+ flag as 'Rule-Only'"]
    end

    Pass --&gt; Output["Return recommendation&lt;br&gt;to Dashboard"]
    RuleOnly --&gt; Output</pre>
</div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<h3 local-id=3D"ed63428b3726" id=3D"TechnicalProposal-SmartHealthCheckupRec=
ommendationDashboard-10.4.2SafetyRuleCategories">10.4.2 Safety Rule Categor=
ies</h3>
<p local-id=3D"9d55f35aa5ca">All safety rules are <strong>configurable via =
the Master Data Management UI</strong> (=C2=A78.1.3, TOR =C2=A73.4.6) witho=
ut requiring code changes. Rules are version-tracked and require maker-chec=
ker approval before activation.</p>
