er leaves hospital premises</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"5e4f546b-a28d-4ca6-9c61-64e5830dc29f" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"a3b487072ce3">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Requires AWS Bangkok Region=
 (ap-southeast-1) and PDPA data processing agreement</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"91798349-0894-4e11-bec4-e9f901104917">
<td data-local-id=3D"9b43fec6-196e-4efa-849e-f759bf61c871" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"636befc22e99"><strong>Operational Effort</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"222c1ddf-19e8-449f-a229-e94c63285cf5" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"3cd0ec9c12b5">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Hospital IT team manages ha=
rdware, patching, physical security</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"6df4faca-afed-4fed-b1ff-176ae4485b91" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"412e7d6b64ae">=E2=9C=85 AWS manages physical infra, patching=
, power =E2=80=94 hospital manages only Docker containers</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"4988741f-a032-4beb-b697-919975c10ef8">
<td data-local-id=3D"079cbaec-e081-416f-b884-0691a22452d2" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"b4afe215a166"><strong>Scalability</strong></p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"c204bf76-f06f-4c1d-8898-12949a85f051" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"ebd6ad1949a1">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Requires additional hardwar=
e purchase for scaling beyond Year 1 capacity</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"fe31549f-8e8d-45d9-940b-27e8092baaa4" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"8186dfecce32">=E2=9C=85 Scale up/down instantly by changing =
instance type</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"ab05a309-51d6-4e20-89ab-3e7773f091ab">
<td data-local-id=3D"17d985d6-6834-47cb-9c3d-46335333b77a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"3251de322a92"><strong>DR &amp; Availability</strong></p></td=
>
<td data-local-id=3D"5703151a-c2c0-4f6b-b30d-0b808ebdbcdf" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"1328fc40fd47">=E2=9A=A0=EF=B8=8F Single-site =E2=80=94 requi=
res offsite backup discipline</p></td>
<td data-local-id=3D"280c122e-7766-4da1-ad29-41a5bdfee9e1" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"f12eb681863f">=E2=9C=85 Multi-AZ, automated backups, easier =
disaster recovery</p></td>
</tr>
<tr data-local-id=3D"b849418e-9031-4378-8ba8-fa9aa110fd5c">
<td data-local-id=3D"d2e0cc3c-0c14-43d1-9186-f972f2e17d6a" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"494c1ad27242"><strong>Network Latency to AI API</strong></p>=
</td>
<td data-local-id=3D"7eccadd5-9875-485a-96c6-af3fbaa9aea0" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"9b80b961ab3e">Depends on hospital's internet connection</p><=
/td>
<td data-local-id=3D"b0427a15-093b-480f-89c3-672e0e4aa2c8" class=3D"conflue=
nceTd">
<p local-id=3D"4437c15a56cc">Low latency from AWS to Google AI API (cloud-t=
o-cloud)</p></td>
</tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</div>
<blockquote local-id=3D"55954a5e-b3f0-4670-ac45-e842ce1fb6e5">
<p local-id=3D"01a2872b6250"><strong>Recommendation:</strong> For a workloa=
d of 30 healthcare providers generating 900 AI prompts/day, both options ar=
e financially viable with comparable 3-year TCOs ($16K =E2=80=93 $21K). The=
 <strong>AI API cost ($248/month)</strong> represents ~14=E2=80=9318% of to=
tal spend =E2=80=94 moderate but manageable. <strong>On-Premise</strong> is=
 best suited if Navavej Hospital has an existing data center with IT operat=
ions staff and prioritizes absolute data residency control. <strong>AWS Clo=
ud</strong> is best suited if the hospital prefers minimal operational over=
head and values elastic scalability for future growth. In either scenario, =
the infrastructure decision should be driven by data residency and operatio=
nal preferences =E2=80=94 the AI API cost is identical regardless of hostin=
g.</p>
</blockquote>
    </div>
</body>
